ChangeLog for csv

2025-11-29  David

	* Version 1.1.0

	* csv (head): Add +n option to display all but last n data rows
	  Example: csv head +3 shows all rows except the last 3

	* csv (tail): Add +n option to start output at row n (1-indexed)
	  Example: csv tail +3 skips first 2 rows, outputs from row 3 to end
	  This follows POSIX tail convention where +n means "starting from"

	* csv.1: Updated man page with +number documentation and examples

	* README, NEWS: Updated documentation

2025-11-25  David

	* Version 1.0.0 released

	* csv: Initial implementation with head, tail, wc, cut commands

	* csv (head, tail): Add -a flag to include header and comment lines

	* csv (wc): Add -a flag to include header in row count
	  Without -a, only data rows are counted (excludes header)

	* csv (cut): Add -a flag for header output, make -f optional
	  When -f is omitted, reads from stdin

	* csv: Add support for comment lines starting with # at file start
	  Comment lines are preserved and output with header when -a is used

	* csv: Add proper error handling for file not found, permission denied

	* csv.1: Man page created

	* Makefile: GNU-compliant makefile with install/uninstall targets
